cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lysos: An open-source generative drug designer for antimicrobial resistance"
message: "If you use Lysos in academic work, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Rajpurohit
    given-names: Rahul
    email: rahulrajpurohitk@gmail.com
type: software
date-released: 2026-05-04
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
url: https://github.com/Rahul-Rajpurohitk/lysos
repository-code: https://github.com/Rahul-Rajpurohitk/lysos
keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - drug design
  - generative ai
  - reinforcement learning
  - gemma
  - amd
  - mi300x
abstract: >-
  Lysos is an open-source generative drug designer specialized for designing
  novel antibiotics against drug-resistant bacteria. It is built on Google's
  Gemma 4 31B large language model, fine-tuned with reinforcement learning
  using publicly verifiable rewards (predicted MIC, drug-likeness,
  synthesizability, hemolytic safety, novelty). Training runs entirely on a
  single AMD Instinct MI300X GPU, leveraging its 192 GB HBM3 memory to keep
  the policy, reference, and reward models coresident during GRPO updates.
  The training pipeline integrates 31,855 instruction-tuning examples drawn
  from ten real public sources (ChEMBL, DBAASP, DRAMP, CARD, PDB, ZINC, and
  others) and an embedding-based novelty signal computed against a 20,489-row
  index of known antibiotics. Lysos was built for the AMD Developer Hackathon
  (May 4-10, 2026).
